<section class="opportunity-section" id="opportunity">
  <div class="s-label reveal">The Opportunity</div>
  <h2 class="s-title reveal stagger-1">What Changes When You Stop Resizing<br>and Start <em>Regrading</em></h2>
  <div class="opp-grid">
    <div class="reveal stagger-2">
      <p class="s-body" style="margin-bottom:24px">There is a technique professional designers use that almost no beginner-to-intermediate crocheter is ever taught. It is called <strong>grading between sizes</strong>. Instead of picking one size and stretching it to fit everywhere, you treat each section of the garment as its own puzzle piece.</p>
      <p class="s-body" style="margin-bottom:24px">Medium shoulders. Large bust. XL hips. Each part gets the size it actually needs — and the transitions between them are blended so smoothly that the finished garment looks like it was designed for you from the start.</p>
      <p class="s-body">That is the core of what the Perfect Fit Formula teaches. It is not pattern drafting. It is not math-heavy design theory. It is a step-by-step system built around one idea: <strong>your pattern is a flexible guide, not a fixed rulebook.</strong></p>
    </div>
    <div class="opp-visual reveal stagger-3">
      <div class="opp-icon">📐</div>
      <p style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:18px;color:var(--brown);margin-bottom:24px;line-height:1.6">Picture this. You find a pattern you love. You sit down for one evening, run it through the system, and know — before you cast on — exactly how it will fit.</p>
      <div class="opp-steps">
        <div class="opp-step"><div class="opp-num">1</div>Measure & diagnose the pattern</div>
        <div class="opp-step"><div class="opp-num">2</div>Isolate the sections that need adjusting</div>
        <div class="opp-step"><div class="opp-num">3</div>Apply targeted changes that respect the stitch repeat</div>
        <div class="opp-step"><div class="opp-num">4</div>Crochet with certainty. Try it on. It fits.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
